      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Jays",
        "body": "The Toronto Blue Jays' first-half finish reeks of missed opportunity, a six-game-under-.500 stumble that has left them 12 games behind in the AL East with their record at 45-51. <strong>Falling to the Padres 5-4 on Sunday, then 8-7 the night before, capped a ugly two-game loss streak that erased any momentum from their lone win in the San Diego series</strong>. The offense, which once flashed contender DNA, has gone quiet - scoring just 11 runs over those final two losses while committing key defensive lapses. Santiago Espinal and Bo Bichette have been solid, but the bullpen imploded again, surrendering critical late-inning leads. With Miles drawing the start tonight against the White Sox, the Jays need a reset <strong>as they open a three-game home series against Chicago at 7:15 PM ET, a must-win stretch to avoid sinking further from the wild-card hunt</strong>.",
        "updated": "Updated July 17, 2026"
